{
  "lesson_id": "b2_compound_adjectives_in_english",
  "level": "B2",
  "title": "Compound adjectives in English",
  "description": "Compound adjectives объединяют два или более слова, которые вместе описывают noun.",
  "theory": {
    "rule_id": "RULE-B2-31-RU",
    "lesson_num": 31,
    "title": "Правила: Compound adjectives in English",
    "level": "B2",
    "overview": "Compound adjectives объединяют два или более слова, которые вместе описывают noun.",
    "main_rule": "Частые patterns: well-known, full-time, user-friendly, high-speed, ten-year-old. Перед noun обычно используется hyphen.",
    "form": "word-word + noun. number + singular noun + adjective ending.",
    "when_why": "Используем compound adjective как одно определение перед noun; часто нужен hyphen.",
    "examples": "a well-known company. → известная компания.\na full-time job. → работа на полный день.\na user-friendly interface. → удобный для пользователя интерфейс.\na five-year-old child. → пятилетний ребёнок.\na high-quality product. → высококачественный продукт.",
    "special_cases": "В number-based compound noun remains singular: five-year-old, not five-years-old. После noun: The child is five years old.",
    "common_mistakes": "❌ a ten-years project → ✅ a ten-year project.\n❌ The child is five-year-old. → ✅ The child is five years old.",
    "dont_confuse": "Перед noun compound acts as one adjective. After noun можно использовать обычное plural time expression.",
    "quick_summary": "compound adjective before noun → often hyphenated.\nnumber + singular noun.\nAfter noun → normal plural form."
  },
